(   - Simple Past + Explicit Chronological Anchor: When a sentence specifies an author, publication) Tj
T*
(   year, or historical date, the Simple Past is grammatically mandatory:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Sanger et al. developed dideoxy chain-termination sequencing in 1977.") Tj
T*
(   - Incorrect: "*Sanger et al. have developed dideoxy sequencing in 1977.") Tj
T*
(   - Present Perfect + General Unanchored Consensus: When referencing ongoing discoveries or) Tj
T*
(   collective knowledge without anchoring them to a discrete moment:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Numerous laboratories have successfully adapted Sanger sequencing for) Tj
T*
(   high-throughput diagnostics.") Tj
T*
(   - Simple Present for Enduring Theories:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The central dogma of molecular biology states that genetic information flows from) Tj
T*
(   DNA to RNA to protein.") Tj
T*
() Tj
