/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 12:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the Mandative Subjunctive in formal institutional, clinical, and laboratory safety protocols.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Nature of the Mandative Subjunctive:) Tj
T*
(   In formal academic and regulatory English, verbs expressing recommendations, mandates, demands,) Tj
T*
(   or necessity \(e.g., demand, insist, require, recommend, suggest, mandate, decree\) governing a) Tj
T*
(   'that'-clause require the bare base form of the verb \(subjunctive mood\) for all grammatical) Tj
T*
(   persons.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Syntactic Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - [Subject] + [Mandative Verb] + that + [Subject] + [Base Verb].) Tj
T*
(   - Note: The verb drops the third-person singular suffix -s and uses the bare base 'be' for the) Tj
T*
(   copula.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Applied Institutional Protocols in Biotechnology:) Tj
T*
(   - Example 1 \(Biosafety Directive\):) Tj
T*
(   - Indicative \(Incorrect\): "The Biosafety Officer requires that every researcher wears nitrile) Tj
T*
(   gloves.") Tj
T*
(   - Subjunctive \(Mandatory\): "The Biosafety Officer requires that every researcher wear nitrile) Tj
T*
(   gloves.") Tj
T*
(   - Example 2 \(Passive Mandative with 'Be'\):) Tj
T*
(   - Indicative \(Incorrect\): "The protocol dictates that the autoclave is decontaminated daily.") Tj
T*
(   - Subjunctive \(Mandatory\): "The protocol dictates that the autoclave be decontaminated daily.") Tj
T*
(   - Example 3 \(Negative Subjunctive\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The SOP recommends that the culture not be exposed to direct ultraviolet radiation.") Tj
T*
(   \(Notice: 'not be exposed', not *is not exposed\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 13:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the sequence of tenses in reported speech and explain the 'Universal Truth' exception in biology papers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Canonical Rule of Backshifting:) Tj
T*
(   When an introductory reporting verb is in the past tense \(e.g., stated, reported, observed,) Tj
T*
(   demonstrated\), verbs in the subordinate reported clause typically shift backward into a past) Tj
T*
(   tense form:) Tj
T*
(   - Direct: "The gene expression is elevated." -> Reported: "The authors reported that the gene) Tj
T*
(   expression was elevated.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Universal Scientific Truth Exception:) Tj
T*
(   When the reported proposition represents a timeless universal law, immutable biological fact,) Tj
T*
(   or currently accepted scientific truth, backshifting is suspended to maintain scientific) Tj
T*
(   veracity:) Tj
T*
(   - Historical Proposition: "Aristotle believed that the heart was the center of intellect.") Tj
T*
(   \(Backshift used because the belief is obsolete\).) Tj
T*
(   - Scientific Truth: "Harvey demonstrated that blood circulates through closed vascular) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
