/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the syntax and semantic difference between 'If I was' and 'If I were' in academic discourse.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mood vs. Tense in English:) Tj
T*
(   - 'If I was': Indicative past tense. Used when referring to an actual historical past) Tj
T*
(   possibility that may indeed have been true:) Tj
T*
(   - "If I was absent from the lab meeting yesterday, it was because the HPLC column was) Tj
T*
(   clogging." \(The speaker may genuinely have been absent\).) Tj
T*
(   - 'If I were': Subjunctive past tense. Used to express pure counterfactual, hypothetical) Tj
T*
(   present or future unreal states that are contrary to fact:) Tj
T*
(   - "If I were the principal investigator of this genomics laboratory, I would reallocate) Tj
T*
(   resources toward cryo-EM instrumentation." \(The speaker is not the PI; the proposition is) Tj
T*
(   counterfactual\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Subjunctive Imperative in Scientific Peer Review:) Tj
T*
(   Scientific speculation, peer review recommendations, and theoretical modeling require strict) Tj
T*
(   adherence to the counterfactual subjunctive 'were' to demarcate hypothetical thought) Tj
T*
(   experiments from empirical realities.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 20:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the Present Continuous tense: valid applications in live monitoring vs. common stylistic errors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Legitimate Deployment in Real-Time Bioprocess Monitoring:) Tj
T*
(   The Present Continuous \(is/are + V-ing\) is fully appropriate when describing live, ongoing) Tj
T*
(   kinetic phenomena currently transpiring during active observation:) Tj
T*
(   - "Real-time sensor logs confirm that cell density is currently doubling every 90 minutes.") Tj
T*
(   - "Under fluorescence microscopy, the phagosome is visibly fusing with the lysosomal vesicle.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Illegitimate Stylistic Creep in Static Descriptions:) Tj
T*
(   Students often mistakenly use the present continuous to describe static structural) Tj
T*
(   characteristics, experimental designs, or written figures:) Tj
T*
(   - Flawed: "Figure 3 is illustrating the reaction kinetics.") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "Figure 3 illustrates the reaction kinetics.") Tj
T*
(   - Flawed: "The plasmid is containing two restriction sites.") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The plasmid contains two restriction sites.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
