T*
(   2. Past Reference Frame:) Tj
T*
(   - Antecedent Action \(Past Perfect\) + Subsequent Action \(Past Simple\):) Tj
T*
(   - "After the researcher had calibrated the pH electrode, she initiated the enzymatic) Tj
T*
(   titration.") Tj
T*
(   - "The fermentation proceeded smoothly until the dissolved oxygen level dropped below critical) Tj
T*
(   threshold.") Tj
T*
(   - Note: When 'before' or 'after' establishes unambiguous temporal priority, both verbs may) Tj
T*
(   stand in Past Simple:) Tj
T*
(   - "After the researcher calibrated the pH electrode, she initiated the titration.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Future Reference Frame:) Tj
T*
(   - Independent Clause \(Future Simple\) + Dependent Time Clause \(Present Simple\):) Tj
T*
(   - Never use future tense in the time clause:) Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical: "We will harvest the biomass as soon as the optical density will peak.") Tj
