(>> Solution to Question 24:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the rules governing conditional sentences expressing concession \('even if', 'whether...or'\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concessive Conditional Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   Concessive conditionals assert that the proposition in the matrix clause remains true) Tj
T*
(   regardless of whether the condition in the subordinate clause is satisfied:) Tj
T*
(   - Even if: Introduces an extreme or unfavorable hypothetical condition that fails to overturn) Tj
T*
(   the main outcome:) Tj
T*
(   - "Even if the reaction temperature drops to 20 deg C, the immobilized biocatalyst remains) Tj
T*
(   active.") Tj
T*
(   - "Even if the gene were overexpressed tenfold, the transport channel would still saturate.") Tj
T*
(   - Whether...or: Presents exhaustive binary alternative conditions leading to the identical) Tj
T*
(   conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   - "Whether the substrate is derived from natural cane sugar or synthetic dextrose, the) Tj
T*
(   fermentation yield is identical.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Punctuation Rules:) Tj
T*
(   Because concessive conditional clauses are parenthetical and non-restrictive, they are) Tj
T*
(   consistently separated from the matrix clause by commas.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the past subjunctive in hypothetical comparison clauses introduced by 'as if' and 'as though'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Syntactic Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   Clauses introduced by 'as if' or 'as though' describe a situation by comparing it to an) Tj
T*
(   imaginary or counterfactual state:) Tj
T*
(   - Subjunctive 'Were' for Unreal Present:) Tj
T*
(   - "The mutant cell line proliferates as if it were immortal.") Tj
T*
(   - Analysis: The cell line is not genuinely immortal, but its phenotypic behavior simulates) Tj
T*
(   immortality. The subjunctive 'were' explicitly signals counterfactual simulation.) Tj
T*
(   - Past Perfect for Unreal Past:) Tj
T*
(   - "The protein precipitate dissolved as though it had never aggregated.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Contrast with Indicative \(Plausible Fact\):) Tj
T*
(   When the speaker believes the condition may actually be true, the indicative mood is retained:) Tj
T*
(   - "The culture broth smells as if it is contaminated." \(The speaker suspects actual bacterial) Tj
T*
(   contamination\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
